```mdl
verdict IdeogramImageGenerationService: The /generate call and errors match; the mapping drops resolution, style type and image-safety.
  status: partial
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-ideogram/src/services/ideogram-service.ts#makeIdeogramGenerationService, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-ideogram/src/services/ideogram-client.ts#generateWithIdeogram, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-ideogram/src/services/ideogram-mapping.ts#mapIdeogramResponse]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-ideogram/src/services/ideogram-mapping.test.ts]
  walkthrough:
    - The service exposes a synchronous generate that hands the request and key to the client. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-ideogram/src/services/ideogram-service.ts#makeIdeogramGenerationService
    - The client builds the image_request body, sends Api-Key through the CORS proxy and raises typed errors. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-ideogram/src/services/ideogram-client.ts#generateWithIdeogram
    - The mapper turns data entries with a url into image/png variants with a Generation record. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-ideogram/src/services/ideogram-mapping.ts#mapIdeogramResponse
  note: |
    `mapIdeogramResponse` maps url, prompt, seed, model (default `V_2`), `requestId` and `createdAt`, but never
    `resolution`, `style_type` or `is_image_safe`, and it drops url-less entries. The spec's `metadata` bag is
    flattened into `generation.requestId` / `generation.createdAt`.
```

